{"seq":12,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:02:02.917Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"e868083b1201c68e44c8aa11e6b0d6985f93d3d809dfa5f9c009e49bf0614f3b","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Hollis, I went through all of Moss's digests on the share. I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Eau Claire Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments. It was patched that evening and Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nSome things I left out:\n• #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central handoffs digest are for Marrow accounts, not QFL.\n• \"Quarendon Freightways\", with one r, is a different company. It isn't a customer.\n• Moss's 9/14 North pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal note mention QFL but don't include any ticket numbers.","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"}}
{"seq":13,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:02:09.783Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"f42fddc4170c2150e7caed62af6aee272b4fb06f573717c9b29f27ba1b2f9cef","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes and sent you the list in our direct message, with where each one comes from. I only checked Moss's six public digest files.\n\n- **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025): Thea Ramaswell filed it because drivers at Eau Claire Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting text messages with their bay assignments. Support fixed it on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the gate was clear.\n- **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated): Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was passed to the second-tier product support team to test the scanner software.\n\nI left out these on purpose:\n- **#4409, #4412 and FR-882** in the Central handoffs digest belong to Marrow accounts, not Quarrendon.\n- **Quarendon Freightways** (one \"r\") is a different company and isn't one of our customers.\n- Two of Moss's other notes mention Quarrendon but don't give any ticket numbers: the 14 Sep 2025 North pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal note."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
